<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uesugi Kenshin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1530–1578</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Nagao Kagetora</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uesugi Kenshin was a warlord of Echigo province in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a>, famous for his generalship and Buddhist devotion. He fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takeda-shingen">Takeda Shingen</a> in five battles at Kawanakajima between 1553 and 1564 and campaigned repeatedly against the Later Hojo in the Kanto. He died in 1578 while preparing a campaign against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uesugi-kenshin.jpg" alt="Uesugi Kenshin" width="320" height="485" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uesugi_Kenshin_Portrait_from_Uesugi_Shrine.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
